WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.137
Done isn't a date.

2
00:00:01.137 --> 00:00:02.862
It's a posture you keep proving.

3
00:00:02.862 --> 00:00:08.006
An instance is closed when five things
hold at once: no usable Windows logins,

4
00:00:08.006 --> 00:00:12.171
SQL authentication refused,
Entra sign-ins observed working,

5
00:00:12.171 --> 00:00:16.662
an Entra identity for the engine,
and multifactor for every person.

6
00:00:16.662 --> 00:00:22.025
Live evidence shows it over a validation
period, and any drift is a violation.

7
00:00:22.025 --> 00:00:27.337
That's why April first, 2027 is
a consequence, not a finish line.

8
00:00:27.337 --> 00:00:31.250
Migration ends well before it, and
the last months are for proving.

9
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:35.736
The decision for data leadership, as
system owner: declare closure only

10
00:00:35.736 --> 00:00:40.450
on the security officer's evidence,
with every exception already accepted.

11
00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:41.860
What could still go wrong?
